ORDINANCE III OF 1962
ORDINANCE III OF 1962
WEST PAKISTAN (BOARD OF
INTERMEDIATE AND
SECONDARY EDUCATION, KARACHI)
ORDINANCE, 1962
2.
Definitions.‑In this Ordinance, unless the context otherwise requires,
the following expressions shall have the meanings hereby respectively assigned
to them, that is to say‑--
(a) "Board" means the
Board of Intermediate and Secondary Education, Karachi, as reconstituted under
this Ordinance ;
(b) "Chairman" means
the Chairman of the Board ;
(c) "College" means an institution within
the jurisdiction of the Board and recognized for the Intermediate Education and
includes a College, having Intermediate and Degree classes and affiliated to
the University for the Degree classes ;
(d) "Committee" means
a committee constituted under this Ordinance ;
(e) "Controlling
of Examination" means the Controller of Examinations of the Board;
(f) "Controlling Authority" means the
Controlling Authority of the Board ;
( g ) "Government" means the Government of West Pakistan;
(h) "Head of an institution" means the
Principal of a College or the Headmaster or Headmistress of a school;
(i) "institution"
means a College or a School;
(j) "Intermediate College" means an
institution recognized for imparting instruction to Class XI and Class XII, and
includes an institution having Intermediate and Secondary classes ;
(k) "Intermediate Education" means
education pertaining to Class XI and Class XII ;
(1) "prescribed"
means prescribed by Regulations or Rules ;
(m) "Principal" means
the head of a College;
(n) "recognised" means recognised by the Board ;
(o) "Regulations" and "Rules"
mean respectively the Regulations and Rules made by the Board under this
Ordinance;
(p) "School" means an
institution recognised only for the Secondary Education ;
(g) "Secondary Education"
means education pertaining to Class IX and Class X and such other classes as
may be declared by Government to be classes of Secondary Education ;
(r) "Secretary" means the Secretary of the Board; and
(s) "University"
means the University of Karachi.

